[{:db/id "q-134163/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6de7a5dd-1335-5904-b3c5-e7953dee13fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134163/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "dfa7bfde-094b-50c1-b6ac-d27e68fff615" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134163/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ff6b1528-ebab-52f2-8ddb-7fbff700fd98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134163/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" :answer/id #uuid "477c9d89-1da4-57fb-bf73-bcfd2fee3e2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134163/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" :answer/id #uuid "fbc2ba8b-103f-5cad-afb8-47da8fa278b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134163/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b91758e8-0361-56ed-bae0-7a111f2d7c0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134163/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" :answer-field/choices ["q-134163/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-134163/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-134163/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-134163/selection/a39e4c3855e119cc134cd501616b2d4242dd33fe6134da1d7da0776d673411f7" "q-134163/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134163" :question/id #uuid "e09a6146-6ce2-509b-a961-b8096bb274f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-134163" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-2,\\,5,\\,1,\\,4},\\,y={-4,\\,2,\\,4,\\,-6}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-2)+5+1+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ((-4)+2+4+(-6)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2\\,-\\,2)(-4\\,-\\,(-1))+(5\\,-\\,2)(2\\,-\\,(-1))+(1\\,-\\,2)(4\\,-\\,(-1))+(4\\,-\\,2)(-6\\,-\\,(-1))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4)(-3)+(3)(3)+(-1)(5)+(2)(-5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+9-5-10] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134163/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134163"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "424e02af-f4a9-58f9-a554-57d66d3b337d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a2402940-7e7a-52bc-9b87-2070ba8256a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "db2a4e14-07b6-52e6-95de-56695dbc4553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "91eeff7f-d3a0-5d4d-ae3b-5fa399a23780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "38fde69f-e301-5595-b0a3-1db051db0c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "19e6146b-0aae-570b-8af5-73b92e65d508" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134159/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-134159/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-134159/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-134159/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-134159/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-134159/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134159" :question/id #uuid "72645700-d4a3-568b-b0a0-cd43ff9b3e63" :question/math-academy-id "q-134159" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-1,\\,6,\\,2,\\,5},\\,y={-2,\\,5,\\,7,\\,6}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=3$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1-3)(-2-4)+(6-3)(5-4)+(2-3)(7-4)+(5-3)(6-4)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-4)(-6)+(3)(1)+(-1)(3)+(2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[24+3-3+4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134159/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-134076"] :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (2+3+(-1)+4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (4+0+2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2-2)(4-3)+(3-2)(0-3)+(-1-2)(2-3)+(4-2)(6-3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(1)+(1)(-3)+(-3)(-1)+(2)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0-3+3+6] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "3d64b483-8edb-5149-8842-f24a15d405a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "da48ce4c-1657-589a-b46f-8b5e3b40f45e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "17828aec-298b-546c-b1fb-3897146ccb81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "3a799b82-a49b-5f08-930a-4abd607cbc93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "05844aaa-f0ea-5ba0-87fe-d8ddf446f955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cee887f-e052-5506-af32-e9f4bfbefa71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149616/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-149616/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-149616/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-149616/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-149616/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-149616/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149616" :question/id #uuid "8ea5cea6-ac74-57bd-b531-a5313a9a9126" :question/math-academy-id "q-149616" :question/problem "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={12,\\,7,\\,6,\\,3},\\,y={-4,\\,-6,\\,-4,\\,-2}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=7$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=-4.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12-7)(-4-(-4))+(7-7)(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(6-7)(-4-(-4))+(3-7)(-2-(-4))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(5)(0)+(0)(-2)+(-1)(0)+(-4)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+0+0-8] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149616/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2ac0065-9315-547a-a9cf-c6a5abea1aed"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149616"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-134066"] :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4-2)(6-8)+(-1-2)(3-8)+(0-2)(12-8)+(5-2)(11-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(2)(-2)+(-3)(-5)+(-2)(4)+(3)(3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[-4+15-8+9] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "ba0a489e-d697-57a1-98c4-7ee0a7430f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "4ad8e44c-1870-5794-b5f8-043c3e22b43e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" :answer/id #uuid "9f483b35-8d70-5cd5-9433-ebfeea67b2eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204/selection/7731c9af51b2c33d92792f2597c202100294f6851d8e1d7a2508f8fc3f5f1dd1" :answer/id #uuid "2b7f79c5-732d-5349-91c4-73af9ef2e11d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "dac05f62-31e5-5c6a-8e2e-e750b0495b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d966d4f0-7ef8-51a6-9516-2d05552856e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134204/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-134204/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-134204/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-134204/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" "q-134204/selection/7731c9af51b2c33d92792f2597c202100294f6851d8e1d7a2508f8fc3f5f1dd1" "q-134204/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134204" :question/id #uuid "a7fed5d4-3bcd-519f-bdfd-0ef5f602eac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-134204" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight, in kg ($y$)** | $30$ | $34$ | $38$ | $42$ |\n\nTara plays soccer. The table above shows the ages and corresponding weights of four of Tara's teammates.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=12$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=36.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(10\\,-\\,12)(30\\,-\\,36)+(11\\,-\\,12)(34\\,-\\,36)+(12\\,-\\,12)(38\\,-\\,36)+(15\\,-\\,12)(42\\,-\\,36)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-2)(-6)+(-1)(-2)+(0)(2)+(3)(6)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[12+2+0+18] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134204/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134204"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" :answer/id #uuid "6c64d1b4-c6cf-5924-880c-3e681467fc2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "8d792c5e-c88c-5a0c-9662-2d3e92cf1e1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561/selection/0f5647700b933a18d4c924b388250a52d426eab8923c02afed2168e950a0d65a" :answer/id #uuid "cb5da30f-0d71-5526-9049-aed729fc3af7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "1a6708de-2226-517a-8252-d1db267f48ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "6bf15134-bad2-5cbd-96b4-b60133522f52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fde9dfcc-7842-526a-bcb1-4d3fdca6bd9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149561/selection/0f5647700b933a18d4c924b388250a52d426eab8923c02afed2168e950a0d65a" :answer-field/choices ["q-149561/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" "q-149561/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-149561/selection/0f5647700b933a18d4c924b388250a52d426eab8923c02afed2168e950a0d65a" "q-149561/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-149561/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149561" :question/id #uuid "5a8b19b6-473c-5ece-b5c9-29853f4e074a" :question/math-academy-id "q-149561" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $12$ | $12$ | $14$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Weight, in lbs ($y$)** | $85$ | $90$ | $97$ | $100$ |\n\nMike plays baseball. The table above shows the ages and corresponding weights of four of Mike's teammates.\nCompute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (12+12+14+14) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 52 \\\\  & =13 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (85+90+97+100) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 372 \\\\  & =93\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12\\,-\\,13)(85\\,-\\,93)+(12\\,-\\,13)(90\\,-\\,93)+(14\\,-\\,13)(97\\,-\\,93)+(14\\,-\\,13)(100\\,-\\,93)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-8)+(-1)(-3)+(1)(4)+(1)(7)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8+3+4+7] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 22 \\\\  & =5.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149561/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149561"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212/selection/23c4d9cdccc3b0bd9ea06a9eb5dde58b720ceae45d6141c2b790a41f11744e08" :answer/id #uuid "787f69af-f26b-502d-97d0-9d6198e11534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" :answer/id #uuid "08160a91-c4c9-5fdf-b718-3bbf6edb47f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" :answer/id #uuid "2c631e10-f31e-5a1a-b9c3-f337fcc63909" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212/selection/22111d11c9d3214c7f97110f849bd2a32c0d5484584befc0bf4faeddce0d44c0" :answer/id #uuid "09bd2b12-deaf-5806-a3b1-df6616adc0f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a3b4f8fb-494d-5a70-8728-8689c901d3e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb98824-e5f0-5246-887d-01a4dacb0afa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134212/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" :answer-field/choices ["q-134212/selection/23c4d9cdccc3b0bd9ea06a9eb5dde58b720ceae45d6141c2b790a41f11744e08" "q-134212/selection/9b32bd1c2d85515eb67bf6ed1aa42ff7a66b88544eaafce7b11ad994fbde1d11" "q-134212/selection/d0d01bb2e3e816b9fd6aee47accd74e6df07f3f36fe536db4d7bfbcde2546d68" "q-134212/selection/22111d11c9d3214c7f97110f849bd2a32c0d5484584befc0bf4faeddce0d44c0" "q-134212/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134212" :question/id #uuid "22f79cc9-53e8-5975-ba0e-1f7352fee98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-134212" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $45$ | $39$ | $43$ | $37$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **IQ Score ($y$)** | $90$ | $82$ | $75$ | $85$ |\n\nThe table above shows the ages and corresponding IQ scores of some of Jerry's colleagues. Compute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (45+39+43+37) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 164 \\\\  & =41 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (90+82+75+85) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 332 \\\\  & =83\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(45\\,-\\,41)(90\\,-\\,83)\\,+\\,(39\\,-\\,41)(82\\,-\\,83)\\,+\\,(43\\,-\\,41)(75\\,-\\,83)\\,+\\,(37\\,-\\,41)(85\\,-\\,83)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(4)(7)+(-2)(-1)+(2)(-8)+(-4)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[28+2-16-8] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134212/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134212"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/