n/math-academy-id "q-134221" :question/problem "| **Age, in years ($x$)** | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Shoe Size (USA) ($y$)** | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $8$ |\n\nMr. Damon recorded the age and shoe size of four tennis players at his academy. The table above shows the information he collected. Compute the covariance of the data sets given that the means are $\\overset{―}{x}=10$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=8.$" :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(7-10)(7-8)+(9-10)(8-8)+(11-10)(9-8)+(13-10)(8-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-3)(-1)+(-1)(0)+(1)(1)+(3)(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[3+0+1+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-134221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216/selection/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" :answer/id #uuid "7dff56c0-c25c-52c8-8666-694965934db2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "c8c38b12-42bb-596c-8729-47932419343d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" :answer/id #uuid "fa2008e0-ae40-5538-82cb-9ace9229783c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" :answer/id #uuid "d8a8a514-672f-5215-8c5f-2159396fbed8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216/selection/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e" :answer/id #uuid "d730056a-622f-53a9-922b-b5b1a8066fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "610bd9ea-e98d-5e59-9fb2-ad97b22dd6fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-134216/selection/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e" :answer-field/choices ["q-134216/selection/2341d4beafc19cb7b8396e0b9f21c544ec7f6a786fc846e9361e36afd0b43437" "q-134216/selection/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" "q-134216/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" "q-134216/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" "q-134216/selection/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-134216" :question/id #uuid "884ebce5-07f2-5ea2-8fcf-3e6457f8e084" :question/math-academy-id "q-134216" :question/problem "| **Temperature, in ${}^{∘}C$ ($x$)** | $24$ | $26$ | $24$ | $22$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Lemonade Sales, in $$$ ($y$)** | $180$ | $202$ | $190$ | $140$ |\n\nThe owner of a lemonade stand keeps track of how much they sell in relation to the daily temperature. The table above shows the data they collected over the past four days. Compute the covariance of the data sets." :question/worked-solution "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (24+26+24+22) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 96 \\\\  & =24 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (180+202+190+140) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 712 \\\\  & =178\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(24\\,-\\,24)(180\\,-\\,178)\\,+\\,(26\\,-\\,24)(202\\,-\\,178)\\,+\\,(24\\,-\\,24)(190\\,-\\,178)\\,+\\,(22\\,-\\,24)(140\\,-\\,178)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(2)+(2)(24)+(0)(12)+(-2)(-38)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+48+0+76] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 124 \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-134216/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cee807c1-dd86-5b0e-a595-5c5754c47e4c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-134216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
